# Chicken Fajitas

Based on [Little Spice Jar](https://www.littlespicejar.com/best-ever-chicken-fajitas) ([wayback](http://web.archive.org/web/20251206221020/https://www.littlespicejar.com/best-ever-chicken-fajitas/)) and [Homesick Texan](https://www.homesicktexan.com/chicken-fajitas-recipe) ([wayback](http://web.archive.org/web/20251027220421/https://www.homesicktexan.com/chicken-fajitas-recipe/))

{ rating="3" image="fajitas.jpg" }
:::
:::

## Ingredients

### Marinade

- [ ] 3 Tbsp [lime juice]{ ing="lime-juice" }
- [ ] 3 Tbsp [pineapple juice]{ ing="pineapple-juice" } (no sugar added)
- [ ] 2 Tbsp [Worcestershire sauce]{ ing="worcestershire-sauce" }
- [ ] 2 Tbsp [avocado or olive oil]{ ing="avocado-or-olive-oil" }
- [ ] 5 cloves [garlic]{ ing="garlic" }, pressed or minced
- [ ] 2 tsp [ground cumin]{ ing="ground-cumin" }
- [ ] 2 tsp [chili powder]{ ing="chili-powder" }
- [ ] 1 tsp [smoked paprika]{ ing="smoked-paprika" }
- [ ] 1 tsp [Mexican oregano]{ ing="mexican-oregano" }
- [ ] 1/2 tsp [onion powder]{ ing="onion-powder" }
- [ ] 2 Tbsp [chopped cilantro]{ ing="chopped-cilantro" }
- [ ] 1 1/2 tsp [salt]{ ing="salt" }
- [ ] 1/2 tsp [black pepper]{ ing="black-pepper" }
- [ ] 1 [jalapeño]{ ing="jalape-o" }, sliced (optional)

### Main

- [ ] 2 lbs [boneless skinless chicken breasts]{ ing="boneless-skinless-chicken-breasts" } or thighs
- [ ] 3 [bell peppers]{ ing="bell-peppers" } (any color), thinly sliced
- [ ] 1 [red or yellow onion]{ ing="red-or-yellow-onion" }, thinly sliced
- [ ] 2 tsp [vegetable oil]{ ing="vegetable-oil" } for cooking

### With

- [ ] 10-12 [flour tortillas]{ ing="flour-tortillas" }
- [ ] [guacamole or sliced avocado]{ ing="guacamole-or-sliced-avocado" }
- [ ] [pico de gallo]{ ing="pico-de-gallo" } or salsa
- [ ] [sour cream]{ ing="sour-cream" }
- [ ] [shredded cheese]{ ing="shredded-cheese" }
- [ ] [lime wedges]{ ing="lime-wedges" }
- [ ] [cilantro]{ ing="cilantro" }

## Recipe

1. Whisk together all marinade ingredients. Add chicken, cover, and refrigerate 4-6 hours (or minimum 1 hour). Remove from fridge 30 minutes before cooking
1. Heat cast iron skillet or heavy skillet over high heat. Add 1 tsp [oil]{ ing="avocado-or-olive-oil" }, then cook half the chicken 3-5 minutes per side until internal temperature reaches 160°F. Rest several minutes, then slice thinly. Repeat with remaining chicken
1. Add 1 tsp [oil]{ ing="avocado-or-olive-oil" } to skillet over high heat. Cook half the [peppers]{ ing="black-pepper" } and [onions]{ ing="red-or-yellow-onion" } until sizzling and slightly charred, 5-7 minutes. Season with [salt]{ ing="salt" } and [pepper]{ ing="bell-peppers" }. Repeat with remaining vegetables
1. Heat [tortillas]{ ing="flour-tortillas" } by cooking each 15 seconds per side over a burner or in a dry skillet until puffed
1. Serve sliced chicken and vegetables with warm [tortillas]{ ing="flour-tortillas" } and toppings so diners can assemble their own

## Notes

- Pineapple juice acts as a natural tenderizer—don’t marinate longer than 6 hours or chicken becomes tough
- For more heat, substitute 4 dried chiles de arbol in the marinade or add sliced jalapeños when cooking vegetables
- Cast iron skillet gives the best char and sizzle

### Instant Pot Variation (No Marinating)

For a quick weeknight version, skip the marinade and use an Instant Pot:

1. Slice chicken thinly and cut peppers slightly thicker. Add to Instant Pot with onions
1. Toss with dry seasonings only: 3 Tbsp fajita seasoning blend (cumin, chili powder, smoked paprika, oregano, onion powder, salt, pepper) and 1 Tbsp oil
1. Add 1/4 cup water. Seal lid, set valve to sealing
1. Pressure cook on high for 4 minutes, then quick release
1. Optional: transfer chicken and vegetables to hot skillet for 2-3 minutes to add char
1. Serve immediately with warm tortillas and toppings

Note: Pressure cooking infuses flavor without marinating.
Save the cooking liquid to make fajita-flavored rice.
